subtests passed.\n\nChanges, all in `more_itertools/more.py`:\n- **`one`**: the too-long path raises `too_long` if it is not `None`, otherwise a `ValueError` with the same message. The empty path raises `too_short` if it is not `None`, otherwise the existing `ValueError('too few items in iterable (expected 1)')`.\n- **`only`**: the too-long path gets the same change. The empty case still returns `default`.\n- The `msg` variable is gone, so the `repr()` message is only built when the default `ValueError` is raised.\n\nDocstrings are unchanged, and I did not touch `more.pyi`, `docs/`, or the test file. I did not run any other checks, since the spec lists only this one.", "ttft_ms": 1256, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 15859, "uuid": "de7a9aac-4777-46e6-b5d4-81904121944f", "ttft_stream_ms": 1149, "time_to_request_ms": 235, "first_content_frame_ms": 1149, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
